<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  NativePHP scaffolds this file with the three JIT/memory entitlements
  Electron and the PHP runtime need, and nothing else. For most apps that is
  right. For one that records, it is the difference between working and
  silently not.

  The hardened runtime checks com.apple.security.device.camera and
  com.apple.security.device.audio-input *before* TCC is consulted. Without
  them a signed app cannot capture and cannot ask to: no prompt appears, and
  the app never shows up in System Settings > Privacy & Security at all. An
  empty list there is not "denied", it is "the request never happened" — and
  it presents exactly like a healthy pipeline that sees nothing. Sonocles paid
  for this lesson (sonocles/docs/ENGINES.md); Rheocles does not pay again.

  The usage strings (NSCameraUsageDescription, NSMicrophoneUsageDescription,
  NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription) are necessary but not sufficient; they live
  in electron-builder.mjs under mac.extendInfo. Both gates have to be open.
  System audio needs the usage string only (docs/PROTOCOL.md § GET /streams);
  screen and windows need neither — ScreenCaptureKit prompts itself.

  This file is also electron-builder's `entitlementsInherit`, which is what
  gets applied to the nested Mach-O binaries inside the bundle — including
  extras/rheocles-core, the process that actually opens the devices. That is
  why the entitlements belong here rather than only on the outer app. Verify
  on the built app AND the nested binary, from the signature, not from here:
      codesign -d --entitlements :- Rheocles.app
      codesign -d --entitlements :- Rheocles.app/Contents/extras/rheocles-core
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
